Design a 4-to-2 priority encoder with a validity output. The module takes a 4-bit input and outputs a 2-bit code corresponding to the highest active input line. The output V indicates whether any of the input lines are high (1 if any input is active, 0 if all are low). If multiple inputs are high, the encoder prioritizes the highest bit according to its position. The default case outputs a 2'b00 if no inputs are high.
