description:
Design a module that implements a non-linear transformation within a 128-bit input state for cryptographic applications. The module takes a 128-bit input (`inDataState`), partitions it into four 32-bit segments, and processes the first two segments (inA0 and inA1) using bitwise operations, including XOR and AND with negated values of the other segments. The transformed results (`inA0new` and `inA1new`) are combined with the unchanged segments (`inA2` and `inA3`) to produce a 128-bit output (`outDataState`). This design is likely part of a larger cryptographic function, contributing to the non-linearity necessary for secure data transformation.
module top_module(
	input wire [127:0] inDataState,
	output wire [127:0] outDataState
);

code:
module top_module(
	input wire [127:0] inDataState,
	output wire [127:0] outDataState
);wire [31:0] inA0;
wire [31:0] inA1;
wire [31:0] inA2;
wire [31:0] inA3;

wire [31:0] inA0new;
wire [31:0] inA1new;

assign   inA0 = inDataState[127:96];
assign   inA1 = inDataState[95:64];
assign   inA2 = inDataState[63:32];
assign   inA3 = inDataState[31:0];

assign inA1new =  inA1 ^ ~inA3 & ~inA2;
assign inA0new = inA0 ^ inA2 & inA1new;

assign outDataState ={inA0new, inA1new, inA2, inA3};

endmodule

