description:
Design a double-register circuit that operates based on two clock signals, SCLK and ECLK. Upon the positive edge of SCLK, it captures the input signals T0 and T1 into a 2-bit temporary register. If the DQSW270 input is active and global set/reset (GSR) is enabled, it resets the output register q_reg to zero. The ECLK clock event transfers the most significant bit of q_reg to the output Q while shifting the register contents to accommodate the next input data. Additionally, upon a reset trigger, if the register set (REGSET) is set to "SET," it resets q_reg to zero, ensuring that the output can be initialized appropriately.
module top_module(
    input T0, T1, SCLK, ECLK, DQSW270, RST,
    output reg Q           // Change output to reg type
);

code:
module top_module(
    input T0, T1, SCLK, ECLK, DQSW270, RST,
    output reg Q           // Change output to reg type
);parameter GSR = "ENABLED";
    parameter REGSET = "SET";

    reg [1:0] t_reg;
    reg [1:0] q_reg;

    always @(posedge SCLK) begin
        t_reg <= {T1, T0};
        if (DQSW270 && (GSR == "ENABLED")) begin
            q_reg <= 2'b0;
        end
    end

    always @(posedge ECLK) begin
        Q <= q_reg[1];
        q_reg <= {q_reg[0], t_reg[1]};
    end

    always @(posedge RST) begin
        if (REGSET == "SET") begin
            q_reg <= 2'b0;
        end
    end
endmodule

